Title:	
ESEM-Within-CFA on Time 1 data

DATA:
FILE IS "ESEM.dat";
!Either identify the data file this way and ensure that is is in the same folder 
!as the input or Indicate the full link to the data file 
!FILE IS "C:\Users\author\Desktop\ESEM chapter\ESEM.dat";

VARIABLE:
! List the name of the variables as they appear in the data file
NAMES ARE X1 X2 X3 X4 X5 X6  Y1 Y2 Y3 Y4 Y5 Y6  GV; 

!If you have an identification variable use the following command where "ID" is 
!the name of this variable 
!IDVARIABLE = ID;
!If you have missing data use the following command where "999" is the code 
!used for missing
!MISSING ARE ALL (999);

!List the variables used in the model
USEVARIABLES ARE X1 X2 X3 X4 X5 X6 ; 

ANALYSIS:
! To identify an alternative estimator, use the following commands
! ESTIMATOR IS MLR;
! ESTIMATOR IS WLSMV;

MODEL:
!Use ESEM results as start values, while fixing the variance to 1 and 
!fixing one cross loading per factor to its ESEM value. 
F1 BY X1*.902 X2*.646 X3*.579 X4*.160 X5*.143 X6@-.039  ;
F2 BY X4*.885 X5*.582 X6*.480 X1@-.041 X2*.218 X3*.344 ; 
F1-F2@1;
[X1*.656 X2*.450 X3*.457 X4*.710 X5*.432 X6*.574];
X1*.391  X2*.290 X3*.538 X4*.400 X5*.313 X6*.504 ;

OUTPUT:
SAMPSTAT STANDARDIZED RESIDUAL CINTERVAL MODINDICES (3.0) TECH2 TECH4;
